good morning  and welcome back to a day in my life  this is a spontaneous vlog  as i've just booked myself in to get a  covert vaccine  medical students as part of the  healthcare team are required to get the  vaccine as soon as possible to protect  both our patients  and ourselves so i thought i'd document  the journey if anyone is curious  it is bright and warm outside but my  heart still pines for the snow we had a  few days ago  i'm on a zoom patient history taking  session in the bus  which unfortunately i cannot contribute  to but still proves quite helpful  i go to the monthly hospital to get my  vaccine and follow the arrows to the  room  my nurse is the sweetest person ever  making me feel almost  normal for asking permission to film the  process something i'd been dreading all  night  [Music]  fantastic and your postcode perfect okay  where are you working at the moment  fantastic okay so just quickly so in  terms of that being probably known  anyway  is the visor and so you'll have to have  the next one  um in twelve weeks absolutely um so the  common side effects are things like  saunas around the site  um you might get you might feel a bit  fatigued might be a bit nauseous um  muscle aches um but just treat that  parasite smile and it should go down you  might start seeing in the next 24 hours  that they will go down  and if you get covered symptoms and  that's not the vaccine so choose it as  covered  um so isolate get test and do what you  need to do with flavoured  um you're not a new year until 14 days  so  you have to wait for them and then  obviously as well  um any questions  right you put this hand in your on your  hip for me oh yes  oh sorry because i'm supposed to hold  that now yep that's okay yeah absolutely  yeah so now um you need to go and sit  down for 15 minutes just so we can  observe you and check you're okay if  there's anything wrong please give us a  shout  and if you feel make sure it's off of  anything  that you're worried about 